## Step 6: We can write $ \cos \left(-\frac{3\pi}{8} \right)$ as $\cos\left(\frac{3\pi}{8} \right)$ because cosine is an even function
\begin{align*}
\left[\frac{2^4}{ 2^2}\right] \left[\cos \left(\frac{\pi}{8} \right) + 2 + \cos \left(\frac{3\pi}{8} \right) \right] \left[2\cos^2 \left(\frac{3\pi}{16} \right)\right]
