## Step 7: Simplify the fraction to become $16$ and use the identity $\left(a+b\right)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$ to expand the squared terms.
We also use $\left( 1 + \cos \theta \right)^2 = 1 + 2\cos \theta + \cos^2 \theta$
\begin{align*}
16 \left[1 + \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{8} \right) + \cos \left(\frac{3\pi}{8} \right) + 2 \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{8} \right) \cos \left(\frac{3\pi}{8} \right)\right] \left[2\cos^2 \left(\frac{3\pi}{16} \right)\right]
