## Step 8: Apply the product-to-sum identity again to $2 \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{8} \right) \cos \left(\frac{3\pi}{8} \right)$
Using the identity, we obtain that $2\cos \left(\frac{\pi}{8}\right) \cos \left(\frac{3\pi}{8} \right) = \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{4}\right) + \cos\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\right) = \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{4}\right)$
