## Step 1: Find the general form of point P
To find the general form of point P, we use the equation of the first line. The general form of a point on the line can be written as $(x, y, z) = (x_0 + at, y_0 + bt, z_0 + ct)$, where $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ is a point on the line and $(a, b, c)$ is the direction vector of the line. For the first line, we have $(x_0, y_0, z_0) = (3, -1, 2)$ and $(a, b, c) = (2, -2, 1)$. Then, point P can be written as $(2t + 3, -2t - 1, t + 2)$.

